From bff7e584a9edb4fc444083b63965e7a5bb6c6aac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:14:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HMI-KEEP: while wb_serve runs, a closed HMI page is reopened
 (5 s without a web page -> open it again)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20260929: "你要一直持續偵測 如果html 被關掉 需要再次開啟 除非C++被關閉".
- tools/wb_serve.cpp (end of file): W906_HmiKeeperTick, called from the main loop on every pump beat (500 ms, same line as the
  State Record Timer2 call). "web page present" = W906_PagesPresent() (live WebSocket or an HTTP request in the last 3 s, the
  MODAL-WAKE definition). 20 s grace after start (the F5 wait page switches to the HMI in that time), then 5 s without a page ->
  open it; no second launch within 30 s; after 3 launches that never connected, every 2 min; any connected page resets it all.
  URL = env W906_HMI_URL (both IOWEB F5 configurations: background.html?mode=debug&machine=HT9050), else ModalWakeUrl (release
  screen). Browser = the default http browser's exe from the registry (the .html association starts nothing on this machine),
  else ModalWakeLaunchEdge. Off with W906_NO_BROWSER_WAKE / --seconds N (g_modalWakeOff, as MODAL-WAKE). Stops with wb_serve.
  Each launch is printed and written to the op log as an HMI line.
- .vscode/launch.json: W906_HMI_URL in both IOWEB configurations.
Syntax-checked (-fsyntax-only, the ship flags). Not built yet: wb_serve was running; the next F5 pre-launch build compiles it.
Not verified on the machine yet (needs EastSun to close the page with wb_serve running).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
